{"assets":["/editorial-assets/7881a7507b1455e1eeccbaf09616abc04ee2f6dbd7de0866a194155a07e2b963.png","/editorial-assets/ac21283952a0def2cc87cb650958528297c03b095e4bbe136cabf1dac2d9d859.png","/editorial-assets/7ab5a704f3ae7bbd17c2ebe639b5c0fea4a2c6b10d2732631c5ef10db7eab6b0.png","/editorial-assets/ceb1cffcc4e1adaec02ddd33e283b1eb72c8aafb2845e904bad38f638db12502.png","/editorial-assets/2745c0e1ae08237a0b1154b0513867c91f6aa01ece307b9d2e43000265affc12.png","/editorial-assets/34bce991238461f408990b1098f4f3bc08353928923c8a70f5d5b1a1699a5e94.png","/editorial-assets/a1f32ba9da7a031bb468aa463cc842c7178605f14400f17715fe54519faa2af4.png","/editorial-assets/038673d10e08cc5192185d5f1e9192b809176cb0c2c524f49c3a9ed2583a88bb.png","/editorial-assets/4e678fccd5e86d5c69be4b18879efa2ccb2bf8915e8d0a161912f014bed5574f.png","/editorial-assets/2f42e48a7ab0e90ac4be479c3f1e8bc841b1477f1f3b39a9a14555f72308b722.png","/editorial-assets/8c55db9f2c8c5081dd83db99a1d011223080aa1bcf095259cdf91299b26557c8.png","/editorial-assets/053439eee74a9756781f5fa874f3eeb48c88e9ce8c6db7fbb06c68287e11d8cf.png","/editorial-assets/924c53a8e73491865569331be96fab2efe2e280f37524259f3b4bd99b4e4ac85.png"],"contestId":"708","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"709A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/709/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"709A - Juicer"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem you have to carefully implement exactly what it written in the statement. Pay attention to some details: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Don't forget to throw away too large oranges. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Don't mix up strict and not-strict inequalities. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Code"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"int main() {\n  int n, b, d;\n  std::cin >> n >> b >> d;\n\n  int current_size = 0;\n  int result = 0;\n  int x;\n  for (; n > 0; --n) {\n    std::cin >> x;\n    if (x > b) {\n      continue;\n    }\n    current_size += x;\n    if (current_size > d) {\n      ++result;\n      current_size = 0;\n    }\n  }\n\n  std::cout << result << \"\\n\";\n  return 0;\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"709B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/709/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"709B - Checkpoints"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sort all point by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-coordinate."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If we've chosen the set of points we want to visit, then we must go either to the leftmost of them and then to the rightmost, or to the rightmost and then to the leftmost, the others will be visited automatically during this process. The other observation is that it makes sense to not visit only either the leftmost or the rightmost point — otherwise this point will be visited during any walk which visits "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 points. So, the solution is to fix the points which we don't want to visit — either the leftmost or the rightmost, after that iterate over two possible orders of visits of the lefmost and rightmost points of the remaining set of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 points and relax the answer. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Also don't forget the case "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1 — then you don't need to visit any point."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Code"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"const int MAXN = 100000;\n\nint x[MAXN];\n\nint main() {\n  int n, A;\n  scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &A);\n  if (n == 1) {\n    printf(\"0\\n\");\n    return 0;\n  }\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    scanf(\"%d\", &x[i]);\n  }\n  int first_max = -2e6;\n  int second_max = -2e6;\n  int first_min = 2e6;\n  int second_min = 2e6;\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    if (x[i] > second_max) {\n      second_max = x[i];\n      if (second_max > first_max) {\n        swap(second_max, first_max);\n      }\n    }\n    if (x[i] < second_min) {\n      second_min = x[i];\n      if (second_min < first_min) {\n        swap(second_min, first_min);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  printf(\"%d\\n\", min(first_max - second_min + min(abs(A - first_max), abs(A - second_min)),\n                     second_max - first_min + min(abs(A - second_max), abs(A - first_min))));\n\n  return 0;\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"708A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/708/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"708A - Letters Cyclic Shift"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If string consists only of symbols 'a', then we could only make it lexicographically bigger. To achieve the least change we should shift the last symbol. In any other case we could make string lexicographically less. We should shift first biggest subsegment of string consists only from symbols not equal to 'a'."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Code"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"void solve() {\n  string s;\n  cin >> s;\n  for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); ++i) {\n    if (s[i] == 'a') {\n      continue;\n    }\n    int j = i + 1;\n    while (j < s.length() && s[j] != 'a') {\n      ++j;\n    }\n    for (int r = i; r < j; ++r) {\n      --s[r];\n    }\n    cout << s << \"\\n\";\n    return;\n  }\n\n  s.back() = 'z';\n  cout << s << \"\\n\";\n\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"708B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/708/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"708B - Recover the String"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Using "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" easy to calculate "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" – numbers of 0 and 1 in string (it could be done by binary search or solving quadratic equation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1) / 2 = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). But in case "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not fixed and could be equal 0 or 1. One could consider both cases for sure (or code several 'if's to throw away one of the variants). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≠ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", then answer is impossible. Otherwise it is possible to create such string using greedy algorithm. Consider string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"string"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", '0') + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"string"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", '1'), its array of subsequences equals {"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", 0, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"}. One could swap neighbouring pairs 01 one by one and transform it to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"string"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", '1') + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"string"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", '0') (similar to bubble sorting), its array equals {"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", 0, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"}. During this process string corresponding to array {"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"} was reproduced exactly once, because every swap reduce "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" by one and increase "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" by one, so we have "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") solution. One could make it linear: take string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"string"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", '0') + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"string"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", '1') and move its zeros one by one directly in the end of string while "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". When "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" become "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" we will move next zero on "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" symbols left and finally get desired string. There is another way to do it, when you build lexicographically smallest string one symbol by one from the beginning."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Code"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"void imp() {\n  cout << \"Impossible\\n\";\n  exit(0);\n}\n\nll invtriange(ll x) {\n  ll l = 1, r = 1000000;\n  while (r - l > 1) {\n    ll m = (l + r) / 2;\n    if (m * (m - 1) / 2 > x) r = m;\n    else l = m;\n  }\n  if (l * (l - 1) / 2 != x) {\n    imp();\n  }\n  return l;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  vvl a(2, vl(2));\n  for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i) for (int j = 0; j < 2; ++j) {\n    cin >> a[i][j];\n  }\n  if (a[0][0] + a[0][1] + a[1][0] + a[1][1] == 0) {\n    cout << \"0\\n\";\n    return 0;\n  }\n  ll c0 = invtriange(a[0][0]);\n  ll c1 = invtriange(a[1][1]);\n  if (a[0][0] == 0 || a[1][1] == 0) {\n    if (a[0][1] + a[1][0] == 0) {\n      if (c0 == 1) c0 = 0;\n      if (c1 == 1) c1 = 0;\n      cout << string(c0, '0') << string(c1, '1');\n      return 0;\n    }\n  }\n  if (c0 * c1 != a[0][1] + a[1][0]) {\n    imp();\n  }\n  string s(c0 + c1, '0');\n  for (int i = 0; i < s.size(); ++i) {\n    if (c0 == 0 || a[0][1] < c1) {\n      s[i] = '1';\n      a[1][0] -= c0;\n      --c1;\n    } else {\n      a[0][1] -= c1;\n      --c0;\n    }\n  }\n  cout << s << endl;\n  return 0;\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"708C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/708/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"708C - Centroids"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first observation is that to make vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" a centroid we need to choose some subtree not containing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with size not exceeding "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/7881a7507b1455e1eeccbaf09616abc04ee2f6dbd7de0866a194155a07e2b963.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" (assume its root is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), remove an edge "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"uw"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" between its subtree and the remaining tree, and add an edge between "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", in such a way that subtrees of all children of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" have size not exceeding "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/7881a7507b1455e1eeccbaf09616abc04ee2f6dbd7de0866a194155a07e2b963.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the centroid of the tree, let's make it a root. Assume "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" are the neighbours of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" are the subtrees of these vertices. Then it is easy to prove, that if some vertex "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ac21283952a0def2cc87cb650958528297c03b095e4bbe136cabf1dac2d9d859.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be made a centroid after replacing one edge of the tree, then it can be done using one of the following options: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Remove some edge "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"vu"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≠ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and add an edge "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xu"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind"